<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIAN BOURSE CAPITALISATION ROSE 2ND WEEK IN A ROW.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIAN BOURSE CAPITALISATION ROSE 2ND WEEK IN A ROW.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse rose to 5.380 billion litas last week from 5.329</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					 July 07-11   June 30-July 04</p>
<p>    Submitted orders	     14,296		16,367</p>
<p>    Executed orders		945		   1,106</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)	  711		   938</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL  2,840,120	   3,431,680</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)	    116		   83</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	11,323,770	  9,321,960</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week  47,292,878	  59,467,564</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week  6,081,934	   5,094,725</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	2,454,740	   1,991,520</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	11,323,770	  9,321,960</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	6		     18</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week    385,380	     1,440,160</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
